    "body": "> > if we have a pending blur path, fire blur at the lowest node in that path that's still connected, and nullify the pending blur path.\n> \n> What happens if the node had been moved to a different tree at that point?\n\nPossibly the lowest node in the path that's still in the main document tree?\n\nPerhaps a cleaner alternative is to create a `Range` initialized at the removed element's parent. It will fall back while its ancestors are removed until it reaches something that's definitely connected at the `update the rendering time`, and will not care if an element is re-inserted.\n\n(The algorithm I put here is a strawman btw, the point is to fire `blur` *somewhere* so that a11y tools that rely on that even can act)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/5416313584/reactions",
