    "updated_at": "2026-08-30T14:17:52Z",
    "body": "Perhaps a better set of steps:\n- A document has a `previously focused range`, a live range or null\n- When removing a focused element, set `previously focused range` to a live range whose root is that element's parent\n- At the beginning of the focusing steps, if `previously focused range` is not null, then fire focusout etc on that range's root (with that surviving root as `relatedTarget` as well) and nullify\n\nAs an alternative, we can fire a `focusreset` event on the body whenever focus fixup is invoked.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
