    "created_at": "2026-08-26T11:59:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-26T11:59:18Z",
    "body": "> if we have a pending blur path, fire blur at the lowest node in that path that's still connected, and nullify the pending blur path.\n\nAt first I liked firing `blur` at the document a little better (if another element hadn't been refocused in the meantime), since that feels less arbitrary. But if we fired it as low in the tree as we can, I suppose anyone listening for `blur` on the document would still hear it, and `e.target` would give the listener more context as to where in the tree blur took place, right? That seems pretty good.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
