    "created_at": "2026-08-26T15:58:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-26T15:58:02Z",
    "body": "Firing `blur` on an element that was not blurred seems like a band-aid rather than desirable behavior. And what about the `relatedTarget`? \n\nFiring `focusout` is maybe more reasonable but not sure it would handle the compat. issue?\n\nIt would also be nice to unify whatever happens here with how other potentially pending events are handled on removed elements. For example, blink and gecko/webkit also disagree on firing `change` on a removed input ([see example](https://codepen.io/editor/Steve-Orvell/pen/01a03ec0-a6b2-7827-9b88-a67e22953fe4)).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
