    "created_at": "2026-08-26T16:03:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-26T16:03:35Z",
    "body": "> Firing `blur` on an element that was not blurred seems like a band-aid rather than desirable behavior. And what about the `relatedTarget`?\n\nBut it was blurred in a way. At the very least it's lost its `focus-within`. But maybe that's more like `focusout`.\n\n> \n> Firing `focusout` is maybe more reasonable but not sure it would handle the compat. issue?\n\nWell I think those tools might be OK with relying on `focusout`? e.g. the code in [this example](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12842#issuecomment-5415660469) seems to.\n\n> It would also be nice to unify whatever happens here with how other potentially pending events are handled on removed elements. For example, blink and gecko/webkit also disagree on firing `change` on a removed input ([see example](https://codepen.io/editor/Steve-Orvell/pen/01a03ec0-a6b2-7827-9b88-a67e22953fe4)).\n\nOh lovely, another one... :)",
