    "updated_at": "2026-08-30T15:26:13Z",
    "body": "A few examples from the wild that can befit from this:\n- Redactyl (see above)\n- Radix: https://github.com/radix-ui/primitives/blob/main/packages/react/focus-scope/src/focus-scope.tsx#L122-L165\n- Focus Trap: https://github.com/focus-trap/focus-trap/blob/master/index.js#L981-L1035\n- Material UI: https://github.com/mui/material-ui/blob/master/packages/mui-material/src/Unstable_TrapFocus/FocusTrap.tsx#L360-L377\n\nThe pattern is to use `setInterval` or a `MutationObserver` as a way to circumvent the missing event.\nFIring a `focusout` on the closest surviving ancestor (or firing a global `focusrestet`, or something...) would make this inefficient/hacky workaround unnecessary and we can perhaps finally be interoperable about this.",
